  "notation": "Saf-C 5606.02",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5606.02 Applicability",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5606.02 Applicability.\n\n(a) Pursuant to RSA 263:12, X, nothing in this part shall prohibit a person from transferring, in non-electronic form or format, personal information contained on the face of a license to another person, provided that the consent of the license holder is obtained if the transfer is not to a law enforcement agency.\n\n(b) Nothing in this part is construed to prohibit the recording, retaining or storing of personal information that is obtained solely from a source independent from the driver’s license, such as the individual him or herself, where the visual inspection of the driver’s license is used to corroborate the personal information.\n\nSource. #7813, EXEMPT, eff 1-1-03",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5600.html"
}
